script = ExtResource("1_8k50v")
fish_name = "Fish With Legs"
grade = 4
sprite = ExtResource("2_138un")
catch_blurb = "Uh oh, we got a runner!"
description = "Doesn't it just look so...wrong? Well, I'm sure you won't be surprised to hear that this freak resulted from a radiation spill that affected waters throughout the planet. F.I.S.H.E. scientists were working on developing a [redacted] for future use in the tournament. They could never have predicted that the chemicals and metallic ores they imported from distant planets with vastly different ecosystems would react together in a toxic way—how could anyone guess? Nonetheless, the unexpected reaction produced large clouds of poisonous gas, and gallons of contaminated runoff that disrupted Pollywood’s natural environment*. And when the [redacted] exploded, radioactive goo and scrap metal were catapulted into tournament waters. Native Pwaaga and tournament staff alike were in uproar over the damage, but the F.I.S.H.E. scientists were able to mitigate most harm to intelligent life.

While it’s unclear why exactly this incident caused such an odd mutation, plenty of theories have tried to explain its existence. A popular one attests that the radiation exposure reverted the fish's genetic code to attribute itself to an entirely different species. However, the radiation spill was so catastrophically large that we can't begin to comprehend how it affected these specific fish on a biological level. So, through the lovely sense of sight, we can observe: these fish have legs. They can walk as any other bipedal animal could, but it seems to be a disadvantage for this species, considering they’re still unable to breathe air. In fact, it's common to see them dead on land on account of their accidentally running too far out of water and perishing before returning to their habitat. Due to this, finding one still alive in the water is quite the rarity, and catching one fresh out of the pond gives you something to brag about. Just, uh, be careful around the legs, they pack quite a kick.

*Some Pwaaga “Druyip ecologists” claim that F.I.S.H.E. industrial production had already damaged the ecosystem of planet “Druyip” (Pollywood to most modern folk) beyond repair, and afterwards continued to do so. However, officials deny this claim—and really, where’s the proof?
"
